From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] schedsvc: another host does not take a person's Run request

Run on a person's task is passed to their task host (1173): the service
notes the request and wakes every host; each marks the requests it has
seen as taken in its own HKCU. A host marked every request, its own tasks'
or not -- so another host under the same account (another person's tasks
run with --as, the shell's own host beside one started by hand) could
mark the person's request first, and the person's host then found it
taken and never ran it. taskrun-gate failed at random on this ("Run on a
person's task did not run it").

A host now marks only the requests for its own tasks.

Test: test/taskrun-gate.sh step 10 (mutant SG_MUTANT_TAKEN_BY_OTHER_HOST
in taskrun.c fails it).
---
--- a/dlls/schedsvc/taskrun.c
+++ b/dlls/schedsvc/taskrun.c
@@ -1123,7 +1123,19 @@
         size = sizeof(taken);
         if (!RegGetValueW(mine, NULL, name, RRF_RT_REG_QWORD, NULL, &taken, &size) && taken >= when) continue;
         EnterCriticalSection(&cs);
-        if ((task = find_task(name)) && task->ours && task->enabled && !task->disabled)
+        task = find_task(name);
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_TAKEN_BY_OTHER_HOST
+        /* Stained Glass OS: a request is marked taken only by the host whose
+         * task it is. Another host of the same account (another person's
+         * tasks run under it with --as, or a second sign-in) marked it too,
+         * and the owner's host, finding it taken, never ran it. */
+        if (!task || !task->ours)
+        {
+            LeaveCriticalSection(&cs);
+            continue;
+        }
+#endif
+        if (task && task->ours && task->enabled && !task->disabled)
         {
             TRACE("Run asked for %s\n", debugstr_w(name));
             start_task(task, TRUE);
